<article class="env-lemma" id="04CV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04CV">Lemma <span data-tag="04CV">76.7.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Then $\Omega _{X/Y}$ is a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a diagram as in Lemma <a href="/tag/04CU" data-tag="04CU">76.7.3</a> with $a$ and $b$ surjective and $U$ and $V$ schemes. Then we see that $\Omega _{X/Y}|_ U = \Omega _{U/V}$ which is quasi-coherent (for example by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/08S2" data-tag="08S2">29.33.7</a>). Hence we conclude that $\Omega _{X/Y}$ is quasi-coherent by Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03M0" data-tag="03M0">66.29.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>